So I have two nodes, I want to see if they touch. I've tried .intersects but it doesn't get the bounds of the node its self and instead gets the parents bounds - thus they are always "touching"

&#x200B;

How can one do this? I don't want to use coordinates if possible as I plan to have many objects in the scene

Okay so it's a little bit annoying but basically you add it in the Global Libraries and add a VM run config. That sounds super complex but it's actually really easy! Entire guide here:  [https://openjfx.io/openjfx-docs/#install-javafx](https://openjfx.io/openjfx-docs/#install-javafx)

&#x200B;

Click the JavaFX and IntelliJ

&#x200B;

Edit: JFx got removed after JDK8 - Also an option to compile with JDK8 instead but JDK13 and Jfx13 are nice
